# External review, round 9 (fresh reviewer; condensed record)

Received 2026-11-09 on the round-9 package (21 files, all read). The reviewer had no earlier-round context.

- **Verdict:** WEIS 2027 4/5 weak accept (60%), AAMAS main 2/5 (25%), EC 1/5 (8%). Every requested headline number
  reproduced at the paper's precision (Q1, Q2, Q4, W0, H4, lottery rows, all five eligibility tallies).
- **Problems, ranked:** (1) doubled-search winners reverse fresh3's C* - R3 sign (-0.038 to +0.015); pooled D2+H3 0.021
  to 0.030 (analysis on existing records). (2) The gain does not identify the value of free replacement; a reset-on versus
  reset-off experiment is needed (needs compute). (3) "Not materially better" depends on the margin; print absolute
  gains, name the comparator's selection objective (text). (4) Uncertainty conditions on six markets and frozen policies;
  the fresh1 extreme Q2 intervals (text, already disclosed). (5) Show fixed interior lottery weights (existing records).
  (6) Lemma 2 proves audit exposure, not a monetary charge; promote the honest-replacement profile; i.i.d. keys in the
  proof. (7) Corollary 1 needs the reverse inequality. (8) The decision-prediction exemptions matter (dropping them gives
  1/2/15); keep Table 19 in the supplement.
- **Related work:** add Gilpatric, Vossler and Liu (2015), JEBO 119:182-196, doi 10.1016/j.jebo.2015.08.006 (verified via
  Crossref).
- **Presentation:** the venue version should keep the core mechanics, theory, Q1/Q4, one factorial plot, one welfare
  panel, and the honest-replacement figure; move prediction scores and matrices to a supplement; mark inherited flags in
  Table 8's decision column.
- **Score movers:** WEIS: honest turnover's burden and benefit; AAMAS: reset-on/off best responses with independent
  restarts; EC: a payoff or welfare theorem for age versus history targeting.

